Z||000001||FieroJoe||03-21-2001||09:25 PM||||An engine tap could be one of many things.  Where do you think the tapping is coming from?  could be bearings, rods, rockers, valves, who knows.  use a rolled up piece of paper or a hose as a stethoscope to try and find out exactly where the tap comes from.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||03-21-2001||09:31 PM||||Depends on the tap.<BR>But if you don't look into it, it could turn into a death knock...<BR>But again, it would give you a reason to put in that V6 or V8 you always wanted!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ed||03-22-2001||01:00 AM||||The cam/timing gears also get noisy.  I had mine replaced years ago when I had the four cylinder recall done.<P>I asked why they were noisy.  They get noisy because they wear as they are some kind of synthetic material. I asked why didn't Pontiac use metal to reduce wear, and the mechanic responded because they were noisy!   ||||reg||1
